order-10c stage 1 type-first audit (2026-08-23)

Decision
  ACCEPT an additive witness_validator design for
  generation.proliferation_morphism. The existing zero-argument/keyword Bool
  method remains regression-only compatibility behavior and cannot itself be
  evidence for the Lean structure. No implementation was performed in stage 1.

Baseline
  Full G3 passed before the audit and after model-evaluation editing stopped:
    logs/gates/order-10c/G3-baseline-20260823.log
  The model-evaluation files were not modified by this audit.

Q1. Lean field classification
  External binders parent and child are proof-carrying DC values. A finite Julia
  bridge must independently validate their DC obligations and complete carriers.

  Record : Type u
    Type parameter, not an obligation.
  Heritage : Type u
    Type parameter, not an obligation; a finite encoding needs a complete
    Heritage carrier to validate total functions and predicates.
  parent_config : Config (dcToOpenSystem parent)
    Candidate data. It encodes S x (S x S) and must belong to that complete
    product carrier.
  child_config : Config (dcToOpenSystem child)
    Candidate data, with the analogous S' x (S' x S') membership check.
  record : Record
    Candidate data. No later ProliferationMorphism field constrains it.
  parent_viable : dcViable parent parent_config
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. It must instead be recomputed
    as parent_config.1 = parent.s.
  child_viable : dcViable child child_config
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. Recompute child_config.1 = child.s.
  parentHeritage : Config (dcToOpenSystem parent) -> Heritage
    Candidate function data. Validate it on the complete parent configuration
    product and require every result to lie in the Heritage carrier.
  childHeritage : Config (dcToOpenSystem child) -> Heritage
    Candidate function data, validated on the complete child configuration product.
  heritageRelated : Heritage -> Heritage -> Prop
    Candidate predicate data. Its finite encoding must be total and Bool-valued
    on the complete Heritage x Heritage carrier.
  heritage_lax : heritageRelated ...
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. Recompute the predicate at the
    two independently computed heritage images.
  Rank : Type u
    Type parameter, not an obligation; finite validation needs a complete carrier.
  rank_preorder : Preorder Rank
    Proof-carrying candidate structure. The runtime le relation is candidate
    data, but accepting reflexivity/transitivity flags would be an oracle. Check
    Bool totality on Rank x Rank, reflexivity on every rank, and transitivity on
    every rank triple.
  parent_rank : Rank
    Candidate data; require carrier membership.
  child_rank : Rank
    Candidate data; require carrier membership.
  wstar : Rank
    Candidate data; require carrier membership.
  child_rank_le_wstar : rank_preorder.le child_rank wstar
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. Recompute with the validated le.
  phi_rich_lax : phi_rich parent <= phi_rich child
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. Recompute both scores.
  branch_transport : forall parent motor satisfying Act and Branch, exists a
    child motor satisfying Act and Branch
    Proof obligation/oracle if supplied as Bool. Recompute over complete finite
    motor carriers.

Q2. Independent recomputation plan
  parent_viable / child_viable
    Validate tuple shape and state-carrier membership, then compare the fast
    component to the corresponding DC's distinguished state. This is exactly
    Generation.dcViable; slow and environment components do not affect viability.

  heritage_lax
    Evaluate the validated total heritage functions at the two candidate configs,
    then evaluate the validated Bool-valued heritageRelated relation on that pair.

  child_rank_le_wstar
    After exhaustive finite preorder validation, evaluate le(child_rank, wstar).

  phi_rich_lax
    There is no Julia function presently implementing Generation.phi_rich.
    Existing primitives Act and is_branch_point match Hinge.Act and
    Richness.Branch on supplied finite relations. Add a local finite score that
    returns 1 iff any motor in the complete motor carrier is both in Act and a
    branch point, otherwise 0. Compare parent_score <= child_score. This matches
    the Lean if-then-else definition under complete-carrier and faithful-relation
    assumptions; no caller phi_rich_lax Bool is accepted.

  branch_transport
    Compute parent Act and child Act from the two supplied finite DC encodings.
    For every m in the complete parent motor carrier, if m is in parent Act and
    is_branch_point(parent.alpha_rel,m), require that some m' in the complete
    child motor carrier is in child Act and is_branch_point(child.alpha_rel,m').
    This directly evaluates the forall/implication/exists nesting. It is vacuous
    when no parent motor satisfies both premises, exactly as in Lean.

  parent DC / child DC and totality
    Reuse the finite check_DC path for the four DC proof fields. Additionally
    reject duplicate/incomplete carrier encodings, out-of-carrier relation images,
    non-Bool predicate/order results, malformed configs, and non-total callbacks
    on every point demanded by the finite products.

Q3. Feasibility and assumptions
  No field is intrinsically noncomputable on complete finite carriers. The Lean
  noncomputable phi_rich becomes decidable by exhaustive finite enumeration.
  The design is infeasible without complete M, M', E, E', C, C', S, S',
  Heritage, and Rank carriers and faithful equality/relation encodings; those
  must be manifest assumptions, not silently inferred. Exceptions from partial
  callbacks must reject the candidate rather than be accepted as evidence.

Q4. Classification
  Target classification: witness_validator, not exact_finite_decision. The
  additive method validates one supplied finite encoding of a
  ProliferationMorphism witness. It does not decide existence for arbitrary Lean
  types and does not establish a global Julia-to-Lean representation bridge.
  complete_only and sound_only do not describe the supplied-witness contract;
  regression_only remains correct only for the legacy Bool-keyword method.

