Q6. Implementation estimate
  Medium-large, but bounded: one additive typed method plus finite validation
  helpers in src/generation.jl, exhaustive positive/mutated tests in
  test/test_generation.jl, and one manifest row reclassification. Expected
  implementation/test size is roughly 200-300 lines across 3 primary files,
  plus the audit/basis log. Catalog, fixed public names, legacy method, exact
  registry, numerical assumptions, formal Lean files, and contract count need
  no change. G1/G2/target G3/connected manifest/full G3/G4 must then be rerun.

Stage-2 guardrails
  Do not accept any of the six Prop fields as supplied Bool evidence.
  Do not weaken, replace, or delete the legacy regression method or its tests.
  Do not claim an inverse ViableSystem-to-DC translation.
  Do not identify ViableSystem.viable with DC.
  Do not add target-layer axioms or write selector state back to individuals.
  Any new finite-carrier/equality premise is a manifest assumption, not a
  relaxed tolerance or an implicit universal claim.

Stage 2 implementation result
  ACCEPT and complete. The legacy Boolean-keyword method is unchanged. An
  additive method accepts only candidate data: two finite ERIEState encodings,
  complete parent/child carrier records, complete Heritage and Rank carriers,
  and a closed ten-field candidate record. Unknown/missing fields, duplicate
  carriers, and observable incomplete carriers are rejected.

  The six Lean Prop fields are never supplied as Bool values. The checker
  independently recomputes parent_viable, child_viable, heritage_lax,
  child_rank_le_wstar, phi_rich_lax, and branch_transport. Heritage callbacks
  are range-checked on every S x (S x S) configuration; heritageRelated is
  required to be Bool-valued on the full Heritage square. rank_le is required
  to be Bool-valued on the full Rank square, reflexive on every point, and
  transitive on every Rank triple.

phi_rich type correspondence
  Lean Generation.phi_rich returns Nat and, by definition, has value 1 exactly
  when RichnessWitness is inhabited and 0 otherwise. Julia
  _generation_phi_rich returns Int and is restricted by construction to the
  same literal values 0 and 1. It receives no candidate score. It calls the
  existing Act and is_branch_point implementations and enumerates the complete
  supplied motor carrier before returning the score.

Equivalent proof fields
  Let RW(dc) abbreviate exists m, m in Act(dc) and Branch(dc.alphaRel,m).
  phi_rich_lax is false exactly when phi_rich(parent)=1 and
  phi_rich(child)=0, hence exactly when RW(parent) and not RW(child).
  branch_transport is forall m, parentWitness(m) -> exists m',
  childWitness(m'). Its consequent does not mention m, so it is equivalent to
  RW(parent) -> RW(child) and has the same false condition. Therefore the two
  fields are logically equivalent under the current Lean definition; they
  cannot be independently falsified without accepting proof oracles. The tests
  execute and assert both calculation paths on one shared false fixture and a
  distinct vacuously-true equivalence fixture. This also records that the field
  named branch_transport establishes existence preservation, not a relation
  between a particular parent m and child m'. Whether a stronger transport
  relation is intended remains a theory-owner decision and was not changed.

Negative evidence
  Four isolated obligation mutations:
    parent_viable=1, child_viable=1, heritage_lax=1,
    child_rank_le_wstar=1.
  Equivalent richness obligations:
    one shared parent-rich/child-nonrich counterexample separately asserts
    phi_rich_lax=false and branch_transport=false, and checker rejection;
    one distinct parent-nonrich/child-nonrich mutation separately asserts both
    paths true (vacuous equivalence regression).
  Encoding mutations:
    unknown field=1, missing field=1, duplicate carrier=1,
    observable incomplete carrier=1.
  The positive candidate and every expected outcome are literal test data; no
  expected value is generated from the public checker.

